1
00:00:16,047 --> 00:00:17,446
(Premium Joss Paper Clothing)

2
00:00:17,447 --> 00:00:19,447
Hing, I need to talk to you.

3
00:00:24,247 --> 00:00:25,647
You really know what I like.

4
00:00:26,247 --> 00:00:29,087
Green is lucky for me. Thank you.

5
00:00:33,287 --> 00:00:35,127
Is there something wrong?

6
00:00:36,327 --> 00:00:38,087
Ms. Mui doesn't
want your inheritance.

7
00:00:40,687 --> 00:00:41,726
Why?

8
00:00:41,727 --> 00:00:43,607
You lied to her for so long
when you were alive.

9
00:00:44,007 --> 00:00:46,007
She's very disappointed.
She doesn't want anything.

10
00:00:47,367 --> 00:00:50,047
I know she suffered a lot
because of me.

11
00:00:50,967 --> 00:00:53,727
I truly want
to leave everything to her.

12
00:00:53,807 --> 00:00:54,967
Can you help me?

13
00:00:55,287 --> 00:00:56,727
When Ms. Mui told me about it,

14
00:00:57,007 --> 00:00:58,407
she had already thought it through.

15
00:00:59,367 --> 00:01:01,807
She's adamant about not fighting
with your daughter.

16
00:01:06,807 --> 00:01:08,287
When my ex-wife
was pregnant with her,

17
00:01:09,487 --> 00:01:10,607
I had just gone bankrupt.

18
00:01:12,447 --> 00:01:14,287
My wife wanted
a divorce immediately.

19
00:01:15,807 --> 00:01:16,887
All these years,

20
00:01:17,727 --> 00:01:19,767
my daughter never cared about me.

21
00:01:21,407 --> 00:01:23,367
But after I died,

22
00:01:23,447 --> 00:01:25,407
she immediately showed up
to fight for the estate.

23
00:01:26,087 --> 00:01:28,887
I don't want to give her everything.

24
00:01:29,047 --> 00:01:30,687
I beg you, please help me.

25
00:01:32,767 --> 00:01:34,447
I can try to talk to Ms. Mui again.

26
00:01:35,447 --> 00:01:37,287
But the final decision is up to her.

27
00:01:37,807 --> 00:01:39,767
If she refuses,
there's nothing I can do.

28
00:01:44,247 --> 00:01:45,247
There's one thing...

29
00:01:46,847 --> 00:01:47,927
If she finds out,

30
00:01:48,887 --> 00:01:50,407
she might change her mind.

31
00:02:01,967 --> 00:02:03,847
I help you, and you help me, right?

32
00:02:04,527 --> 00:02:05,607
Of course.

33
00:02:06,207 --> 00:02:07,727
I want you to do
one more thing for me.

34
00:02:10,727 --> 00:02:12,207
Chan Fat refuses to confess.

35
00:02:12,447 --> 00:02:14,327
We only have
Shum Wai Lok's statement.

36
00:02:14,607 --> 00:02:15,903
Are we really going
to prosecute him?

37
00:02:15,927 --> 00:02:17,006
Go ahead and prosecute him.

38
00:02:17,007 --> 00:02:19,207
Shum Wai Lok's salary is so low.

39
00:02:19,607 --> 00:02:21,647
But after his mom
started dating Chan Fat,

40
00:02:21,727 --> 00:02:22,967
he was able to move out.

41
00:02:23,047 --> 00:02:25,127
Chan Fat is definitely suspicious.

42
00:02:25,447 --> 00:02:26,807
Now that kid won't admit it.

43
00:02:26,887 --> 00:02:29,727
But based on the timing
and their connection,

44
00:02:29,807 --> 00:02:31,527
it's the strongest angle
to charge him.

45
00:02:32,447 --> 00:02:33,487
You're working so hard.

46
00:02:33,727 --> 00:02:35,487
Is it because Chan Fat
offended Officer Poon,

47
00:02:35,567 --> 00:02:36,983
so you need
to show off for your boss?

48
00:02:37,007 --> 00:02:38,046
Shut up.

49
00:02:38,047 --> 00:02:40,647
Go find more evidence
to charge Chan Fat...

50
00:02:40,727 --> 00:02:42,007
if you have the time.

51
00:02:42,087 --> 00:02:43,447
Whatever you say.

52
00:02:44,087 --> 00:02:45,527
It's not that easy to find.

53
00:04:18,047 --> 00:04:20,646
(Episode 12)

54
00:04:20,647 --> 00:04:22,247
(This is a work of fiction.)

55
00:04:22,967 --> 00:04:25,367
What the police have on Chan Fat...

56
00:04:25,607 --> 00:04:26,847
is all circumstantial evidence.

57
00:04:27,967 --> 00:04:29,143
I need something more concrete.

58
00:04:29,167 --> 00:04:30,567
Something that will finish him off.

59
00:04:30,807 --> 00:04:34,007
Is there any way to prove
the goods were delivered to him?

60
00:04:35,607 --> 00:04:38,127
Lok said Chan Fat never
went upstairs for the handovers.

61
00:04:38,847 --> 00:04:40,247
They always met on the street.

62
00:04:41,327 --> 00:04:43,287
Sometimes Chan Fat would
pick up Lok in his car,

63
00:04:43,367 --> 00:04:44,847
and they would
do the handover inside.

64
00:04:45,607 --> 00:04:47,287
I'll go scout around Lok's building.

65
00:04:48,007 --> 00:04:50,287
I'll also ask Lok
where Chan Fat usually drove him.

66
00:04:51,567 --> 00:04:53,087
I need you
to do something else for me.

67
00:04:55,727 --> 00:04:57,607
This is Chow Kwai Hing's daughter,
Chow Suk Yee.

68
00:04:57,967 --> 00:04:59,047
Investigate her background.

69
00:04:59,367 --> 00:05:00,367
Got it.

70
00:05:27,967 --> 00:05:28,967
Sir.

71
00:05:30,807 --> 00:05:31,967
Look at this kid.

72
00:05:32,767 --> 00:05:33,807
He's only 15.

73
00:05:34,527 --> 00:05:36,047
He's being framed
for drug trafficking.

74
00:05:37,127 --> 00:05:38,887
Your shop has CCTV.

75
00:05:39,927 --> 00:05:41,567
You might be his only hope.

76
00:05:41,647 --> 00:05:42,687
Can you help him?

77
00:05:48,927 --> 00:05:49,927
Excuse me.

78
00:05:51,207 --> 00:05:53,047
I saw the CCTV outside your door.

79
00:05:53,127 --> 00:05:54,127
This kid is only 15 years old...

80
00:05:54,128 --> 00:05:56,168
Sorry, we don't let outsiders
view our CCTV footage.

81
00:05:56,687 --> 00:05:58,063
He's being framed
for drug trafficking.

82
00:05:58,087 --> 00:05:59,287
You might be able to help him.

83
00:05:59,327 --> 00:06:00,367
Please leave. I'm sorry.

84
00:07:20,927 --> 00:07:21,927
Hello?

85
00:07:23,327 --> 00:07:26,127
How long do you keep
your CCTV footage for?

86
00:07:26,407 --> 00:07:27,967
We had a burglary before,

87
00:07:28,047 --> 00:07:30,527
so we're in the habit
of keeping it longer.

88
00:07:30,607 --> 00:07:32,127
I think it might go back
to a year ago.

89
00:07:33,207 --> 00:07:34,207
Thank you.

90
00:07:41,967 --> 00:07:43,343
The patient refuses
to take her medicine.

91
00:07:43,367 --> 00:07:45,767
Even changing her saline drip
is a struggle every single day.

92
00:07:46,207 --> 00:07:47,527
It's dangerous if this continues.

93
00:07:48,087 --> 00:07:49,967
Can I sign the consent
for her surgery?

94
00:07:50,407 --> 00:07:51,647
The patient is still conscious.

95
00:07:51,807 --> 00:07:53,007
We still need her own consent.

96
00:07:53,407 --> 00:07:54,407
You should talk to her.

97
00:08:20,207 --> 00:08:21,807
I'll get Lok to plead guilty first.

98
00:08:22,407 --> 00:08:25,087
Once Chan Fat is out
and my aunt agrees to the surgery,

99
00:08:26,447 --> 00:08:28,327
you'll present evidence
of my negligence.

100
00:08:29,287 --> 00:08:31,567
Then we'll get Lok a new lawyer
for an appeal and retrial.

101
00:08:31,727 --> 00:08:33,727
But this will ruin your reputation.

102
00:08:36,447 --> 00:08:37,687
My aunt is running out of time.

103
00:08:38,847 --> 00:08:40,247
This is the best way for everyone.

104
00:08:41,767 --> 00:08:43,087
I hope Lok can understand.

105
00:08:44,127 --> 00:08:45,687
If you hadn't kept looking
for evidence,

106
00:08:45,767 --> 00:08:47,287
he could have
faced 20 years in prison.

107
00:08:47,687 --> 00:08:49,567
Now, he'll be acquitted
after a short stay.

108
00:08:49,767 --> 00:08:50,927
He will understand.

109
00:08:52,127 --> 00:08:53,127
Do you think I should...

110
00:08:53,128 --> 00:08:54,567
tell Lok the whole plan?

111
00:08:55,927 --> 00:08:58,247
From your description,
Lok is quite naive.

112
00:08:59,327 --> 00:09:01,007
Chan Fat has
many informants in prison.

113
00:09:01,767 --> 00:09:03,967
It depends on whether you're willing
to take the gamble.

114
00:09:04,647 --> 00:09:07,207
Fine, then I'll keep him
in the dark.

115
00:09:08,327 --> 00:09:10,207
My only concern now is...

116
00:09:10,607 --> 00:09:13,007
if Chan Fat will really divorce
and let your aunt go.

117
00:09:14,407 --> 00:09:15,847
I'll find a way when the time comes.

118
00:09:17,367 --> 00:09:19,527
I just want my aunt
to have the surgery.

119
00:09:20,167 --> 00:09:21,847
Let me know if you need any help.

120
00:09:23,407 --> 00:09:24,407
Thank you.

121
00:09:25,967 --> 00:09:26,967
Talk to you later.

122
00:09:39,287 --> 00:09:41,407
Although you insist
you knew nothing,

123
00:09:42,447 --> 00:09:44,327
all the evidence points to you.

124
00:09:45,407 --> 00:09:46,927
You were practically
caught red-handed.

125
00:09:48,207 --> 00:09:51,127
The chances of conviction
are very high.

126
00:09:51,887 --> 00:09:53,967
But I didn't do anything!

127
00:09:56,847 --> 00:09:58,247
I can only say you're unlucky.

128
00:09:59,927 --> 00:10:01,967
Some people have
their bags swapped at the airport.

129
00:10:02,047 --> 00:10:03,527
And just like that,
they get 20 years.

130
00:10:04,487 --> 00:10:07,807
Ridiculous things like that
really happen in this world.

131
00:10:10,007 --> 00:10:13,127
What does that mean?
Am I going to prison?

132
00:10:16,727 --> 00:10:18,327
The silver lining is...

133
00:10:19,087 --> 00:10:21,207
you're a first-time offender
with no criminal record.

134
00:10:22,567 --> 00:10:24,767
Pleading guilty reduces
the sentence by one-third.

135
00:10:26,647 --> 00:10:29,207
Good behavior inside
reduces it by another third.

136
00:10:30,247 --> 00:10:31,847
In total, you won't
even serve 10 years.

137
00:10:34,047 --> 00:10:35,487
But if you don't plead guilty now...

138
00:10:35,767 --> 00:10:37,007
and are later convicted,

139
00:10:38,007 --> 00:10:39,327
it'll be at least 20 years.

140
00:10:46,047 --> 00:10:47,407
As your lawyer,

141
00:10:49,327 --> 00:10:50,607
I advise you to plead guilty.

142
00:10:55,927 --> 00:10:57,007
Look on the bright side.

143
00:10:57,887 --> 00:10:59,607
It's much shorter than 20 years.

144
00:11:02,007 --> 00:11:03,087
If I go to prison,

145
00:11:05,287 --> 00:11:06,727
what about my mom?

146
00:11:08,887 --> 00:11:10,327
She's working in the Mainland.

147
00:11:12,927 --> 00:11:15,247
I haven't dared
to tell her what happened.

148
00:11:19,007 --> 00:11:20,287
I'll notify your mother...

149
00:11:21,527 --> 00:11:22,847
and see how I can help her.

150
00:11:33,967 --> 00:11:35,007
How much did you get paid?

151
00:11:35,727 --> 00:11:36,807
What are you talking about?

152
00:11:37,807 --> 00:11:40,047
Didn't you say we had
a definite chance to win this case?

153
00:11:40,207 --> 00:11:42,047
How much did Chan Fat pay you
to deceive him?

154
00:11:43,767 --> 00:11:46,247
I've drafted a will.
Please handle it for me.

155
00:11:46,327 --> 00:11:47,407
I'll go and sign it later.

156
00:11:51,687 --> 00:11:55,007
All this time, I've been
turning a blind eye to what you do.

157
00:11:55,527 --> 00:11:57,047
I thought we were just making money.

158
00:11:57,807 --> 00:11:59,287
If you don't do it,
someone else will.

159
00:12:01,167 --> 00:12:02,567
But my wife is about to give birth.

160
00:12:03,927 --> 00:12:06,007
I don't think I can work with you
for the time being.

161
00:12:24,407 --> 00:12:26,063
I followed Chow Kwai Hing's daughter
for a few days.

162
00:12:26,087 --> 00:12:28,687
She goes to work, leaves work,
and eats all alone.

163
00:12:28,767 --> 00:12:30,223
She doesn't have
any special schedule.

164
00:12:30,247 --> 00:12:32,007
But I found
something quite interesting.

165
00:12:33,407 --> 00:12:34,407
What is it?

166
00:12:35,727 --> 00:12:36,887
She's color-blind.

167
00:12:42,607 --> 00:12:43,646
Excuse me.

168
00:12:43,647 --> 00:12:45,687
I left a paper bag
where I was sitting just now.

169
00:12:45,847 --> 00:12:46,967
Did anyone pick it up?

170
00:12:48,207 --> 00:12:49,807
- Is this it?
- That's the one.

171
00:12:51,727 --> 00:12:52,847
What's inside?

172
00:12:53,447 --> 00:12:55,007
A yellow skirt.

173
00:12:57,007 --> 00:12:58,127
What color?

174
00:12:59,967 --> 00:13:03,447
It's not yellow.
It's dark green, right?

175
00:13:03,687 --> 00:13:04,687
That's right.

176
00:13:04,688 --> 00:13:06,687
I even pretended
to bump into her later.

177
00:13:06,767 --> 00:13:08,887
I dropped some red and green paper.

178
00:13:08,967 --> 00:13:10,407
I even chatted with her for a bit.

179
00:13:10,487 --> 00:13:12,607
She really can't distinguish
between those two colors.

180
00:13:14,007 --> 00:13:16,887
Color blindness in women
is indeed rare.

181
00:13:18,767 --> 00:13:20,887
If it's hereditary...

182
00:13:21,647 --> 00:13:23,007
You really know what I'm thinking.

183
00:13:23,727 --> 00:13:26,527
Green is lucky for me. Thank you.

184
00:13:37,927 --> 00:13:38,927
Where's Ben?

185
00:13:40,647 --> 00:13:41,647
He's hitting on a girl.

186
00:13:51,687 --> 00:13:54,687
Which one do you want? This one?

187
00:13:54,767 --> 00:13:55,887
Why did you choose this one?

188
00:13:55,967 --> 00:13:57,143
Because I was born
in the Year of the Pig.

189
00:13:57,167 --> 00:13:58,607
You were born
in the Year of the Pig?

190
00:13:59,407 --> 00:14:00,727
Say thank you to the big brother.

191
00:14:00,967 --> 00:14:02,167
Thank you, big brother.

192
00:14:04,327 --> 00:14:07,127
These plushies are all
from that lady. Look.

193
00:14:14,087 --> 00:14:15,287
Thank you, miss.

194
00:14:22,967 --> 00:14:24,927
- Bye.
- Bye.

195
00:14:29,447 --> 00:14:30,447
What is it?

196
00:14:33,767 --> 00:14:35,447
Don't try to give me money again.

197
00:14:37,527 --> 00:14:38,527
I'm taking you private.

198
00:14:39,327 --> 00:14:40,687
You won't get a penny from now on.

199
00:14:41,567 --> 00:14:42,567
Are you satisfied now?

200
00:14:48,687 --> 00:14:49,687
What's wrong?

201
00:14:50,527 --> 00:14:52,047
You really know me well.

202
00:14:54,127 --> 00:14:55,127
Go on.

203
00:14:57,087 --> 00:14:58,527
Can you do me a favor?

204
00:15:10,807 --> 00:15:12,607
Sorry, I'm late.

205
00:15:16,567 --> 00:15:19,167
Did you mistake me for someone else?

206
00:15:21,127 --> 00:15:22,607
Although it's
our first time meeting,

207
00:15:23,367 --> 00:15:25,767
you're the most elegant person
in the entire restaurant.

208
00:15:26,447 --> 00:15:27,727
I couldn't have mistaken you.

209
00:15:28,527 --> 00:15:29,847
Monica, I'm John.

210
00:15:30,487 --> 00:15:31,727
Nice to meet you.

211
00:15:33,247 --> 00:15:36,327
I'm not Monica. My name is Elysee.

212
00:15:39,527 --> 00:15:40,527
That's impossible.

213
00:15:44,247 --> 00:15:45,287
This isn't you?

214
00:15:47,607 --> 00:15:49,047
There's a slight resemblance,

215
00:15:49,807 --> 00:15:51,847
but I've never
taken a photo like this.

216
00:16:05,327 --> 00:16:07,047
Looks like I've been stood up.

217
00:16:10,607 --> 00:16:12,647
A woman who drinks vodka alone...

218
00:16:12,767 --> 00:16:13,847
must be very special.

219
00:16:14,687 --> 00:16:15,927
If you don't mind,

220
00:16:16,167 --> 00:16:17,567
how about I buy you a drink?

221
00:16:18,807 --> 00:16:19,927
This is for you.

222
00:16:23,407 --> 00:16:24,407
Thank you.

223
00:16:33,887 --> 00:16:36,407
I only met you
because Monica stood me up.

224
00:16:37,407 --> 00:16:39,087
Thank you.
I had a great time tonight.

225
00:16:40,647 --> 00:16:41,647
Me too.

226
00:16:42,287 --> 00:16:44,207
I haven't talked this much
in a long time.

227
00:16:45,487 --> 00:16:46,767
Sorry, my stomach hurts a bit.

228
00:16:46,847 --> 00:16:47,927
May I use your bathroom?

229
00:16:59,847 --> 00:17:01,207
Sorry, I'll be quick.

230
00:17:02,487 --> 00:17:04,327
It's okay. Take your time.

231
00:17:37,727 --> 00:17:40,287
God, please forgive me.

232
00:17:41,127 --> 00:17:46,567
Forgive me for letting
a virile man inside my room.

233
00:17:47,687 --> 00:17:48,687
I know it.

234
00:17:49,567 --> 00:17:51,407
I know he didn't just want
to use the bathroom.

235
00:17:52,687 --> 00:17:54,847
He must have an ulterior motive.

236
00:17:56,127 --> 00:17:58,887
So please give me a firm heart...

237
00:17:59,287 --> 00:18:02,207
so that I can resist temptation.

238
00:18:05,247 --> 00:18:06,567
- I...
- I'm sorry.

239
00:18:06,687 --> 00:18:07,823
The smell in there is a bit strong.

240
00:18:07,847 --> 00:18:09,847
Wait a while
before going in. Rest early.

241
00:18:29,247 --> 00:18:30,327
It's fine now.

242
00:18:31,927 --> 00:18:33,007
I told you so.

243
00:18:33,367 --> 00:18:34,887
Your niece is amazing.

244
00:18:35,367 --> 00:18:37,567
Where is she?
I really must reward her.

245
00:19:18,127 --> 00:19:19,127
Are you awake?

246
00:19:19,447 --> 00:19:20,447
Yes.

247
00:19:20,887 --> 00:19:21,927
Do you want breakfast?

248
00:19:22,367 --> 00:19:23,367
Sure, I'll cook.

249
00:19:23,727 --> 00:19:24,727
I'll do it.

250
00:20:14,287 --> 00:20:16,367
Dead again? Why am I dead again?

251
00:20:20,407 --> 00:20:21,407
Who is that?

252
00:20:21,408 --> 00:20:23,806
You tricked Shum Wai Lok
into confessing,

253
00:20:23,807 --> 00:20:25,807
causing him
to tragically commit suicide.

254
00:20:26,647 --> 00:20:28,647
How could you
do something so wicked?

255
00:20:28,927 --> 00:20:30,647
Of course you have to die.

256
00:20:31,847 --> 00:20:32,847
Suicide?

257
00:20:33,327 --> 00:20:34,423
Shum Wai Lok didn't commit suicide.

258
00:20:34,447 --> 00:20:35,623
I just talked to him
a few days ago...

259
00:20:35,647 --> 00:20:36,807
He's already dead.

260
00:20:37,407 --> 00:20:39,407
Shum Wai Lok is now in Suicide Hell.

261
00:20:39,487 --> 00:20:41,207
Do you want me
to take you to see him?

262
00:20:44,567 --> 00:20:45,567
No.

263
00:20:48,407 --> 00:20:50,327
That was my plan. I...

264
00:20:51,327 --> 00:20:53,167
I've thought it through. I...

265
00:20:54,247 --> 00:20:55,527
I'll save Aunt first.

266
00:20:55,607 --> 00:20:57,207
Then I'll save Lok...

267
00:20:57,287 --> 00:20:58,287
Shut up!

268
00:20:59,767 --> 00:21:00,903
Even if you wanted
to save your aunt,

269
00:21:00,927 --> 00:21:02,367
this wasn't the way
to do it, was it?

270
00:21:02,927 --> 00:21:04,767
You made
such an innocent boy confess.

271
00:21:04,847 --> 00:21:06,807
Did you ever think about
what would happen to him?

272
00:21:06,887 --> 00:21:08,087
I'm 100 percent certain.

273
00:21:08,167 --> 00:21:09,863
With your brains,
there must have been another way.

274
00:21:09,887 --> 00:21:11,687
You're just used to using
immoral methods.

275
00:21:13,447 --> 00:21:15,327
No, that's not it.

276
00:21:15,407 --> 00:21:16,927
- I'm not...
- Yau Yam Yam.

277
00:21:18,087 --> 00:21:19,687
Do you know
why I let you return to life?

278
00:21:19,727 --> 00:21:21,567
Out of everyone,
I only allowed you to.

279
00:21:26,807 --> 00:21:28,327
Because I didn't
want you to waste...

280
00:21:28,407 --> 00:21:30,447
the lifespan
your grandparents gave you.

281
00:21:32,327 --> 00:21:33,407
What are you talking about?

282
00:21:36,127 --> 00:21:37,927
Actually, you died
when you were five.

283
00:21:44,127 --> 00:21:47,687
(Mistakes Must Be Penalized)

284
00:22:12,207 --> 00:22:15,687
This is bad.

285
00:22:16,527 --> 00:22:17,606
Your Majesty,

286
00:22:17,607 --> 00:22:19,567
there was indeed
a small accident just now.

287
00:22:24,367 --> 00:22:25,887
Only the little girl's time was up.

288
00:22:26,087 --> 00:22:27,343
What are those two
next to her doing?

289
00:22:27,367 --> 00:22:29,167
They just wouldn't let go
for dear life.

290
00:22:29,767 --> 00:22:31,207
Time was up just now.

291
00:22:31,287 --> 00:22:33,807
We know they're quite old,

292
00:22:33,887 --> 00:22:35,807
so we shouldn't be too violent.

293
00:22:36,167 --> 00:22:37,527
What do you mean, too violent?

294
00:22:38,527 --> 00:22:40,063
Do you think
bringing them here to die...

295
00:22:40,087 --> 00:22:41,927
is better than letting them live?

296
00:22:42,007 --> 00:22:43,287
Ridiculous.

297
00:22:44,527 --> 00:22:45,983
Why are you standing there
like a log?

298
00:22:46,007 --> 00:22:47,847
- Send them away!
- Come on, let's go.

299
00:22:47,927 --> 00:22:50,327
- No!
- No!

300
00:22:51,847 --> 00:22:53,167
Is there some mistake?

301
00:22:53,327 --> 00:22:55,247
My granddaughter is still so young.

302
00:22:55,527 --> 00:22:58,327
She can't die before us.

303
00:22:58,767 --> 00:23:00,046
Fate is set.

304
00:23:00,047 --> 00:23:01,423
The Book of Life and Death
does not make mistakes.

305
00:23:01,447 --> 00:23:03,167
Take these two elders away.

306
00:23:03,407 --> 00:23:04,847
- King of Hell!
- No!

307
00:23:05,007 --> 00:23:07,007
I beg you to have mercy.

308
00:23:07,087 --> 00:23:09,247
Please spare my granddaughter.

309
00:23:09,967 --> 00:23:12,767
We'll give you anything you want.

310
00:23:13,647 --> 00:23:16,247
What could two old mortals
possibly give me?

311
00:23:19,807 --> 00:23:20,807
My life.

312
00:23:20,887 --> 00:23:24,007
I'll trade my life for Yam Yam's.

313
00:23:24,687 --> 00:23:26,047
We'll give her our lifespans.

314
00:23:26,247 --> 00:23:28,687
However many years we have left,
we'll give them all.

315
00:23:32,167 --> 00:23:34,407
In all my time as the King of Hell,

316
00:23:35,047 --> 00:23:36,327
this is the first time...

317
00:23:36,407 --> 00:23:38,167
anyone has made such a request.

318
00:23:39,167 --> 00:23:40,647
We're serious.

319
00:23:41,007 --> 00:23:43,007
Please!

320
00:23:43,687 --> 00:23:45,447
My granddaughter is
only five years old.

321
00:23:45,887 --> 00:23:47,847
Do you have the heart
to let a little girl...

322
00:23:48,167 --> 00:23:49,887
die just like that?

323
00:23:51,367 --> 00:23:53,167
We've lived for decades.

324
00:23:53,247 --> 00:23:55,567
A few more years won't
make a difference.

325
00:23:57,007 --> 00:23:58,327
But it's different for Yam Yam.

326
00:23:58,407 --> 00:24:01,887
She's so young
with a long road ahead.

327
00:24:02,967 --> 00:24:07,047
She can grow up to be a good person
and contribute to society.

328
00:24:07,367 --> 00:24:10,127
She deserves to stay up there
more than we do.

329
00:24:15,527 --> 00:24:16,527
Little girl.

330
00:24:18,527 --> 00:24:20,527
Do you know what it means
to contribute to society?

331
00:24:20,567 --> 00:24:21,607
Helping people.

332
00:24:21,967 --> 00:24:24,127
See? She's really smart.

333
00:24:24,207 --> 00:24:25,887
It's such a waste
for her to die so young.

334
00:24:25,967 --> 00:24:28,407
Please give her a chance to live.

335
00:24:34,087 --> 00:24:37,087
There truly is no rule here
for sacrificing one's lifespan.

336
00:24:38,407 --> 00:24:41,607
But no precedent doesn't mean
it can't be done.

337
00:24:45,727 --> 00:24:46,727
Yau Yam Yam,

338
00:24:48,247 --> 00:24:51,047
I'm now transferring
your grandparents' lifespans to you.

339
00:24:51,127 --> 00:24:53,287
Cherish it and be a good person.

340
00:24:53,727 --> 00:24:56,847
Help others
and contribute to society.

341
00:24:57,287 --> 00:24:58,287
Do you understand?

342
00:25:03,687 --> 00:25:07,007
Yam Yam, Grandma
and Grandpa have to go now.

343
00:25:09,367 --> 00:25:11,767
Take good care of yourself.

344
00:25:12,087 --> 00:25:14,767
Live a happy life, okay?

345
00:25:16,767 --> 00:25:20,447
Be a happy and good person, Yam Yam.

346
00:25:20,567 --> 00:25:22,407
Take care of yourself.

347
00:25:30,047 --> 00:25:31,607
How come I don't
remember any of this?

348
00:25:32,807 --> 00:25:34,023
Do you think I'd let a child...

349
00:25:34,047 --> 00:25:35,807
take these memories back
to the mortal world?

350
00:25:39,247 --> 00:25:40,303
Do you know
how many years of life...

351
00:25:40,327 --> 00:25:41,767
your grandparents gave you in total?

352
00:25:44,847 --> 00:25:46,647
It was a full 65 years.

353
00:25:47,087 --> 00:25:48,943
They could have lived
until they were in their nineties.

354
00:25:48,967 --> 00:25:50,463
But they chose
to give that time to you.

355
00:25:50,487 --> 00:25:51,847
Because they believed you could...

356
00:25:51,927 --> 00:25:53,727
do good things for this world.

357
00:25:58,167 --> 00:26:00,447
That was the first time
since I became the King of Hell...

358
00:26:00,967 --> 00:26:04,567
that I felt a sense of hope
for this job.

359
00:26:05,687 --> 00:26:06,927
It was the first time...

360
00:26:07,807 --> 00:26:10,767
I felt I had finally done
something meaningful.

361
00:26:14,367 --> 00:26:15,487
But I was wrong.

362
00:26:16,407 --> 00:26:18,327
You didn't cherish your life.

363
00:26:18,447 --> 00:26:20,207
Because you committed so many sins,

364
00:26:20,287 --> 00:26:22,927
your 70-year lifespan was
cut short to 31!

365
00:26:26,087 --> 00:26:27,527
I wanted to make up for my mistake.

366
00:26:28,047 --> 00:26:30,127
I wanted to prove
that people can change.

367
00:26:30,207 --> 00:26:31,967
I let you return
to accumulate merit.

368
00:26:34,927 --> 00:26:36,447
But you are still incorrigible.

369
00:26:45,687 --> 00:26:46,687
I'm sorry.

370
00:26:56,127 --> 00:26:57,167
According to the handbook,

371
00:26:57,487 --> 00:27:01,687
for your second mistake,
you're demoted to a common ghost.

372
00:27:03,447 --> 00:27:06,127
During this vacuum period
in hell without a king,

373
00:27:06,407 --> 00:27:07,807
I will be in charge.

374
00:27:09,047 --> 00:27:10,767
I am now officially ordering...

375
00:27:11,247 --> 00:27:14,127
that the dead shall never
return to the mortal world.

376
00:27:14,687 --> 00:27:17,487
Lifespans cannot be altered at will.

377
00:27:18,247 --> 00:27:21,967
And you cannot help ghosts
fulfill their last wishes.

378
00:27:22,407 --> 00:27:25,927
Disrupting order
will be severely punished.

379
00:27:28,047 --> 00:27:29,047
Yau Yam Yam,

380
00:27:29,487 --> 00:27:33,487
you have committed too many sins.

381
00:27:34,007 --> 00:27:36,927
I hereby sentence you
to the 18th level of hell...

382
00:27:37,847 --> 00:27:40,327
for a duration of 749 years.

383
00:28:10,967 --> 00:28:11,967
Where did you go?

384
00:28:12,007 --> 00:28:13,287
Did you take my van?

385
00:28:13,367 --> 00:28:15,647
I need it. Come back quickly.

386
00:28:19,607 --> 00:28:22,127
An 18-year-old inmate was found...

387
00:28:22,207 --> 00:28:24,366
hanging in his cell at 8am today...

388
00:28:24,367 --> 00:28:25,503
at the Lai Chi Kok Reception Center.

389
00:28:25,527 --> 00:28:27,127
He was pronounced dead
at the hospital.

390
00:28:27,247 --> 00:28:29,047
The inmate was
arrested last month...

391
00:28:29,127 --> 00:28:31,447
on suspicion of trafficking
dangerous drugs.

392
00:29:52,087 --> 00:29:54,087
The plushies and I will wait
for you to return.

393
00:29:57,447 --> 00:29:59,007
I'll take good care of them.

394
00:30:01,407 --> 00:30:02,847
They'll be kept
in perfect condition.

395
00:30:26,767 --> 00:30:27,767
Is Yam Yam here?

396
00:30:28,127 --> 00:30:29,127
What's the matter?

397
00:30:29,607 --> 00:30:31,207
I called her,
but she didn't pick up.

398
00:30:31,287 --> 00:30:32,807
I have something important
to tell her.

399
00:30:33,527 --> 00:30:35,447
She's sick and sleeping.

400
00:30:36,167 --> 00:30:37,206
I'll go in and check on her.

401
00:30:37,207 --> 00:30:39,647
She said she doesn't want
to see anyone,

402
00:30:40,607 --> 00:30:41,607
including you.

403
00:30:44,607 --> 00:30:46,247
She thinks she looks
too awful right now.

404
00:30:46,927 --> 00:30:48,327
She's not in the mood for visitors.

405
00:30:50,047 --> 00:30:52,207
Then please tell her I came by.

406
00:30:52,287 --> 00:30:53,727
Ask her to call me
when she's better.

407
00:30:56,247 --> 00:30:57,247
Wait.

408
00:31:02,887 --> 00:31:03,887
Be good to her.

409
00:31:22,007 --> 00:31:24,527
(87 Unread Messages,
39 Missed Calls)

410
00:31:35,327 --> 00:31:37,847
(I'm sick and need rest.
(Don't call me.)

411
00:31:41,927 --> 00:31:44,087
Lok is dead. Will it affect me?

412
00:31:44,287 --> 00:31:45,327
Call me back quickly.

413
00:31:47,007 --> 00:31:48,527
Where did your niece go?

414
00:31:48,607 --> 00:31:50,047
She's not answering any of my calls.

415
00:31:50,127 --> 00:31:52,327
Honey, I feel so unwell.

416
00:31:52,847 --> 00:31:55,327
Your Chinese medicine isn't working.

417
00:31:56,327 --> 00:31:58,047
Try calling your niece.

418
00:31:58,287 --> 00:31:59,287
See if she picks up.

419
00:31:59,647 --> 00:32:00,647
Hurry.

420
00:32:10,567 --> 00:32:11,567
No answer.

421
00:32:12,807 --> 00:32:13,807
Darn it.

422
00:32:15,127 --> 00:32:16,127
Honey.

423
00:32:16,447 --> 00:32:18,447
Honey, where are you going?

424
00:32:45,767 --> 00:32:47,607
Help, I'm in so much pain.

425
00:32:47,687 --> 00:32:50,367
Help me.

426
00:32:50,447 --> 00:32:51,847
Help!

427
00:32:53,647 --> 00:32:56,087
Just kill me.
I don't want to stay here.

428
00:32:56,887 --> 00:33:00,647
Let me die. I really want to die.

429
00:33:00,807 --> 00:33:01,807
Shut up!

430
00:33:02,287 --> 00:33:04,903
I'll have the King of Hell shred you
into pieces if you keep it up.

431
00:33:04,927 --> 00:33:06,367
Fine, do it quickly.

432
00:33:06,607 --> 00:33:07,967
It's unbearable here.

433
00:33:09,927 --> 00:33:11,047
Is that what you want?

434
00:33:15,447 --> 00:33:16,767
Well, I'm not going to do it.

435
00:33:22,407 --> 00:33:25,367
If anyone makes a noise,
I'll press this.

436
00:33:25,607 --> 00:33:28,047
I'll sear your organs
until medium-well.

437
00:33:28,607 --> 00:33:30,607
You'll be in agony,
but you won't die.

438
00:33:32,487 --> 00:33:34,287
Keep shouting
and I'll press it again!

439
00:33:45,287 --> 00:33:47,367
Don't think this place is empty,

440
00:33:47,687 --> 00:33:49,967
that it's nothing
and not scary at all.

441
00:33:52,127 --> 00:33:53,247
You're wrong.

442
00:33:53,607 --> 00:33:54,647
Let me tell you.

443
00:33:55,367 --> 00:33:57,687
Having nothing at all is
the scariest part.

444
00:33:58,607 --> 00:34:01,087
Imagine having
to sit here in boredom,

445
00:34:01,167 --> 00:34:03,047
staring into space
for thousands of years.

446
00:34:03,727 --> 00:34:06,287
That is the true horror of hell.

447
00:34:10,567 --> 00:34:11,567
Don't believe me?

448
00:34:13,607 --> 00:34:15,967
You'll find out
after staying a while.

449
00:34:19,287 --> 00:34:21,767
I'm off work. Enjoy yourselves.

450
00:34:45,087 --> 00:34:47,407
So this is where you are, you shrew.

451
00:34:48,167 --> 00:34:49,327
You! It's you!

452
00:34:49,687 --> 00:34:51,207
You got our boss demoted.

453
00:34:51,287 --> 00:34:52,423
And now we're all
being punished for it.

454
00:34:52,447 --> 00:34:54,767
We even have to be guards
in the 18th level of Hell.

455
00:34:55,047 --> 00:34:57,327
Look at him.
Even his horse was melted.

456
00:34:57,407 --> 00:34:58,487
I'm sorry.

457
00:35:00,007 --> 00:35:01,303
I'm sorry
for dragging you into this.

458
00:35:01,327 --> 00:35:03,087
I didn't think it would
be this serious.

459
00:35:03,607 --> 00:35:05,847
We shouldn't talk to her.

460
00:35:06,127 --> 00:35:08,847
Ignore her
and let her die of boredom.

461
00:35:08,927 --> 00:35:11,487
Why don't we try
pressing that button?

462
00:35:11,927 --> 00:35:13,247
We can slow-cook her organs.

463
00:35:13,647 --> 00:35:15,007
Good idea.

464
00:35:15,087 --> 00:35:16,967
Wait.

465
00:35:18,607 --> 00:35:20,367
If you tell me where Lok is,

466
00:35:21,087 --> 00:35:22,607
you can torture me however you want.

467
00:35:22,687 --> 00:35:23,847
You're crazy.

468
00:35:23,927 --> 00:35:25,543
We can torture you
however we want anyway.

469
00:35:25,567 --> 00:35:26,887
Who are you to bargain with us?

470
00:35:27,007 --> 00:35:28,647
You're the one who killed him.

471
00:35:28,727 --> 00:35:30,167
Why do you want to know where he is?

472
00:35:31,487 --> 00:35:32,647
I want to apologize to him.

473
00:35:32,887 --> 00:35:33,887
Apologize?

474
00:35:33,967 --> 00:35:37,727
Apologize to us first, you shrew!

475
00:35:37,807 --> 00:35:39,287
Didn't I already apologize?

476
00:35:39,887 --> 00:35:41,247
How dare you talk back!

477
00:35:43,727 --> 00:35:45,207
Even though I've apologized,

478
00:35:45,807 --> 00:35:48,247
saying it a thousand times...

479
00:35:48,327 --> 00:35:50,047
or a million times isn't enough.

480
00:35:53,487 --> 00:35:59,047
I'm sorry.

481
00:35:59,127 --> 00:36:00,223
- She sure has a way with words.
- I'm sorry.

482
00:36:00,247 --> 00:36:01,247
Fine, that's enough.

483
00:36:01,807 --> 00:36:03,127
I'll tell you where Lok is.

484
00:36:03,447 --> 00:36:05,247
It might make you suffer more.

485
00:36:08,687 --> 00:36:09,887
He's right next door.

486
00:36:10,927 --> 00:36:13,127
Suicide Hell is
right next to the 18th level.

487
00:36:14,127 --> 00:36:16,327
But unfortunately,
even if it's that close,

488
00:36:16,807 --> 00:36:18,167
you'll never be able to apologize.

489
00:36:32,167 --> 00:36:33,647
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

490
00:36:38,847 --> 00:36:40,527
Actually, that King of Hell
was quite nice.

491
00:36:40,567 --> 00:36:41,807
He was very compassionate.

492
00:36:41,967 --> 00:36:43,167
Why was he fired?

493
00:36:44,527 --> 00:36:46,207
He had a thing
with that female lawyer.

494
00:36:46,287 --> 00:36:48,047
Mortals and ghosts cannot
be together.

495
00:36:48,167 --> 00:36:50,447
The Emperor found out
and demoted him.

496
00:36:51,007 --> 00:36:53,087
- No way.
- It's true.

497
00:36:53,967 --> 00:36:56,007
But it makes sense
when you think about it.

498
00:36:56,207 --> 00:36:58,967
Otherwise, why would he
let her return to life?

499
00:36:59,327 --> 00:37:02,327
But the Emperor caught her too.

500
00:37:02,527 --> 00:37:04,127
She was cast
into the 18th level of hell.

501
00:37:05,527 --> 00:37:08,047
What a tragic love story.

502
00:37:08,327 --> 00:37:12,207
I heard she helps ghosts
fulfill their last wishes.

503
00:37:12,767 --> 00:37:14,287
Look, I've saved up
a lot of coins too.

504
00:37:14,887 --> 00:37:16,327
I hope I can find her.

505
00:37:16,487 --> 00:37:19,167
I want her to find a good man
for my wife, Mary.

506
00:37:19,447 --> 00:37:21,367
Then she won't have
to stay a widow for me.

507
00:37:21,687 --> 00:37:22,727
Wait a minute.

508
00:37:23,287 --> 00:37:24,527
Isn't your wife's name Jenny?

509
00:37:27,087 --> 00:37:29,527
One's the wife, one's the mistress.
Don't talk about it.

510
00:37:30,367 --> 00:37:31,503
Whatever you do, don't tell anyone.

511
00:37:31,527 --> 00:37:32,807
Come here. This round is on me.

512
00:37:32,887 --> 00:37:34,007
Treat me to a meal!

513
00:37:34,087 --> 00:37:36,047
Fine, treating you
to a meal is easy.

514
00:37:36,127 --> 00:37:37,767
Come here. I'll be back later.

515
00:37:37,847 --> 00:37:39,447
Hey, what are you doing? Don't go!

516
00:37:42,527 --> 00:37:43,807
You jerk, are you stealing?

517
00:37:44,127 --> 00:37:45,127
It's mine.

518
00:37:45,287 --> 00:37:47,887
Yours? My coins are marked.

519
00:37:47,967 --> 00:37:50,687
I have plenty of money.
My account is just frozen for now.

520
00:37:51,047 --> 00:37:52,943
I'm just borrowing a coin
to handle important business.

521
00:37:52,967 --> 00:37:54,343
When I have money, I'll pay you back
double immediately.

522
00:37:54,367 --> 00:37:55,406
What are you doing?

523
00:37:55,407 --> 00:37:57,887
You steal it
and call it a loan? Save it.

524
00:37:57,967 --> 00:37:58,967
Triple.

525
00:37:59,327 --> 00:38:00,807
Ten times!
I'll pay you back 10 times!

526
00:38:01,807 --> 00:38:03,527
Why should I believe you?

527
00:38:07,087 --> 00:38:08,447
Because I am the King of Hell!

528
00:38:17,687 --> 00:38:19,247
It's him! It really is
the King of Hell!

529
00:38:19,967 --> 00:38:22,087
Well? Do you believe me now?

530
00:38:22,567 --> 00:38:23,567
Your Majesty,

531
00:38:23,807 --> 00:38:25,167
you reduced my sentence back then.

532
00:38:25,367 --> 00:38:26,767
You saved me from the Volcano Hell.

533
00:38:27,007 --> 00:38:29,287
Now that you're in trouble,
I'll definitely help you.

534
00:38:29,447 --> 00:38:30,767
Take these. Do you have any?

535
00:38:31,087 --> 00:38:32,247
Help him out.

536
00:39:11,567 --> 00:39:12,567
Am I dead?

537
00:39:12,887 --> 00:39:14,407
Don't worry, it's just a dream.

538
00:39:14,487 --> 00:39:16,463
You've been by the corpse so long,
your yin energy is very strong.

539
00:39:16,487 --> 00:39:17,607
It's easy for you to see me.

540
00:39:18,007 --> 00:39:19,367
Does that mean Amber can be saved?

541
00:39:21,607 --> 00:39:23,287
This is a difficult matter
to handle.

542
00:39:23,767 --> 00:39:26,287
I know her intentions were good,
but her methods were wrong.

543
00:39:27,527 --> 00:39:28,527
What do you mean by that?

544
00:39:28,687 --> 00:39:30,607
I have a way we can try.

545
00:39:30,687 --> 00:39:31,887
But I'll need your help.

546
00:39:32,767 --> 00:39:33,807
I'll do anything to help.

547
00:39:37,207 --> 00:39:40,047
Finish what Yam Yam originally
wanted to do as soon as possible.

548
00:39:40,127 --> 00:39:41,623
Do your best
to help her accumulate merit.

549
00:39:41,647 --> 00:39:43,607
Reduce her sins as much as you can.

550
00:39:44,287 --> 00:39:45,447
No problem. Anything else?

551
00:39:46,127 --> 00:39:47,383
This is enough
to keep you busy for a while.

552
00:39:47,407 --> 00:39:49,687
I'll take care of the rest.
We'll work on multiple fronts.

553
00:39:50,287 --> 00:39:51,486
Thank you.

554
00:39:51,487 --> 00:39:53,647
But we have to be quick.
We can't hide this for long.

555
00:40:07,727 --> 00:40:08,767
Please sign for this.

556
00:40:37,007 --> 00:40:38,127
Are you all right?

557
00:40:38,367 --> 00:40:40,487
Why did you want
to see me so urgently?

558
00:40:41,007 --> 00:40:42,007
I'm sorry.

559
00:40:43,207 --> 00:40:45,367
Actually, I had an ulterior motive
for approaching you.

560
00:40:45,967 --> 00:40:46,967
What?

561
00:40:49,407 --> 00:40:50,407
Even so,

562
00:40:51,247 --> 00:40:52,887
I truly enjoyed talking to you.

563
00:40:54,367 --> 00:40:56,887
If you could just relax,
you would be much happier.

564
00:40:59,007 --> 00:41:00,047
I'm sorry.

565
00:41:00,607 --> 00:41:02,847
I don't quite understand
what you're saying.

566
00:41:07,567 --> 00:41:09,327
If you're willing
to forgive me later,

567
00:41:10,367 --> 00:41:11,966
you can find me anytime.

568
00:41:11,967 --> 00:41:13,087
I will always listen.

569
00:41:14,807 --> 00:41:15,807
Bye.

570
00:41:27,247 --> 00:41:29,687
I'm sorry. I can notify you
when she has recovered.

571
00:41:29,767 --> 00:41:30,767
Bye.

572
00:41:34,047 --> 00:41:35,047
Hello?

573
00:41:35,247 --> 00:41:37,047
I'm sorry, she's not
in the office now.

574
00:41:37,127 --> 00:41:38,327
I'm her apprentice, Celine.

575
00:41:38,407 --> 00:41:40,607
If you have a message,
I'll pass it to her right away.

576
00:41:41,407 --> 00:41:42,407
Okay.

577
00:41:43,727 --> 00:41:45,087
Okay, thank you.

578
00:41:54,367 --> 00:41:55,703
Master, are you feeling any better?

579
00:41:55,727 --> 00:41:56,903
So many people are looking for you.

580
00:41:56,927 --> 00:41:58,207
I'm about to reach my limit.

581
00:41:58,607 --> 00:41:59,847
Please get back to me soon.

582
00:42:01,887 --> 00:42:04,247
Celine, someone just
brought a document over.

583
00:42:04,327 --> 00:42:06,647
He said it's urgent and must be
handed to you personally.

584
00:42:08,087 --> 00:42:09,087
Who was it?

585
00:42:09,607 --> 00:42:11,607
A handsome young man
in his early twenties.

586
00:42:11,887 --> 00:42:13,143
Before I could ask for his name,

587
00:42:13,167 --> 00:42:14,167
he had already left.

588
00:42:16,007 --> 00:42:18,247
Don't worry, I've checked it.
There's nothing suspicious.
